  "description": "No 16 Seafield Crescent is a handsome bay fronted semi-detached family home (94sqm/1,011sqft) nicely positioned on a corner site in this most desirable and well-established neighbourhood. The accommodation briefly comprises:  Porch, hall, two reception rooms and kitchen.  Upstairs there are 2 double bedrooms and a single bedroom together with a family bathroom.  Outside to the front is a large driveway with plenty of off street car parking leading to the garage.  A side gate leads to the westerly facing rear garden.\n\nThis home offers immense potential to expand the accommodation and benefits from an expired planning permission (ref: D15A/0339) to construct a two-storey side and rear extension if so desired.\n\nSeafield Crescent is a leafy residential road located between the Stillorgan N11 and Rock Road.  The immediate area offers a wealth of local amenities including specialist shops, coffee shops and deli’s and the property is within easy reach of the Merrion and Stillorgan Shopping Centres and Blackrock Village.   The QBC on the N11 and the DART station on the Rock Road provide easy access to the city centre, not forgetting the attractive coastal setting with Booterstown Nature Reserve and Sandymount Strand both within easy walking distance.\n\nACCOMMODATION\n\nPORCH\n\nHALLWAY\nStairs to first floor.\n\nLIVING ROOM\n3.78m x 3.40m \nFeature open fireplace with timber surround and tiled wrought iron inset. Bay window to the front aspect. \n\nDINING ROOM\n3.46m x 4.25m\nSliding patio door to rear garden\n\nKITCHEN\n2.30m x 3.22m\nFitted with wall and base units with countertops over. Stainless steel sink unit. Window to the rear aspect. \n\nFIRST FLOOR LANDING\nAccess to attic. Hot press and window to the side aspect. \n\nBEDROOM 1\n3.50m x 4.22m\nFitted wardrobes and shelving. Bay window to the front aspect. \n\nBEDROOM 2\n3.50m x 3.32m\nWindow to the rear aspect. \n\nBEDROOM 3\n2.25m x 2.64m\nWindow to the front aspect. Fitted wardrobes.\n\nBATHROOM\nBath with Triton electric shower unit. Pedestal wash hand basin and W.C. Window to the rear aspect. \n\nOUTSIDE \nThis property is well set back from the road and enjoys a large front garden with a driveway providing plenty of off street parking. The wide road frontage offers huge potential to extend this property to the side (subject to planning). The front garden is laid mainly in lawn with established perimeter hedging. A gated side entrance opens to the rear garden which enjoys a delightful westerly aspect with plenty of sunshine throughout the day. The rear garden is laid in lawn with a large patio area and has a concrete store shed. \n\nGARAGE \n3m x 4.80m\nUp and over door. Rear pedestrian door. Replaced Idea gas boiler serving the heating system.\n",
